// ============================================================================
// COMPOSITE: NamedPipe_C2_HighConfidence_MTDF
// Author: Ala Dabat | Date: 2026-07-05
// Framework: MTDF (Minimum Truth Detection Framework)
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Sentinel Advanced Hunting
// Maturity: HIGH — near-zero benign overlap on all anchors
// Deployment: Continuous 24/7 monitoring (not a periodic hunt)
//
// ============================================================================
// WHY THIS IS A COMPOSITE, NOT A HUNT OR ROUTER
// ============================================================================
//
// MTDF requires a single Minimum Truth anchor per composite — one
// indisputable fact that cannot exist in a normal enterprise without
// indicating the attack is real.
//
// This composite contains FOUR separate truth anchors. Each one fires
// independently. They share a file because they share the same:
//   - Telemetry source (DeviceEvents NamedPipe*)
//   - Noise domain (near-zero benign overlap for all four)
//   - Output format (MTDF HunterDirective)
//   - Scoring architecture (base = 55+, threshold >= 75)
//
// Per MTDF Split/Keep rules:
//   KEEP when: same truth surface + same noise domain + same telemetry source
//   SPLIT when: truth surface changes / noise domain changes
//
// All four anchors live in the same noise domain (near-zero overlap),
// same truth surface (named pipe events), same telemetry source
// (DeviceEvents). They belong in one composite file.
//
// ============================================================================
// THE FOUR MINIMUM TRUTH ANCHORS
// ============================================================================
//
// ANCHOR 1: ForkNRunHex
//   What it is: Cobalt Strike's Fork-n-Run technique creates a short-lived
//   post-exploitation process and communicates via a dynamically-named pipe
//   whose name is a random 7-10 character hexadecimal string.
//   Pattern: \\.\pipe\[7-10 hex chars]
//   Why it's Minimum Truth: No legitimate enterprise application creates pipes
//   matching this exact regex. The pattern is structurally unique to CS
//   Fork-n-Run. If this pattern exists, the attack is real.
//   Anchoring strategy: SUBSTRATE-FIRST (the pipe NAME IS the signal —
//   no intent inference required, the substrate is the truth)
//
// ANCHOR 2: MojoDeviation
//   What it is: Chrome, Edge, and other Chromium browsers use a named pipe
//   IPC mechanism called "Mojo." Legitimate Mojo pipes follow a rigid format:
//   \\.\pipe\mojo.[PID].[COUNTER].[SUFFIX]
//   Attackers sometimes name their C2 pipes to mimic Mojo (e.g., malleable
//   C2 profiles in Cobalt Strike).
//   Why it's Minimum Truth: A pipe that LOOKS like Mojo but either:
//   (a) doesn't match the legitimate Mojo format, OR
//   (b) is created by a non-browser process
//   has near-zero legitimate explanation in a corporate estate.
//   Anchoring strategy: SUBSTRATE-FIRST (the deviation from known-good format
//   is the substrate truth — the pipe itself is the signal)
//
// ANCHOR 3: EpmTyposquat
//   What it is: The Windows endpoint mapper uses a pipe named "epmapper"
//   for RPC service registration. Attackers sometimes create pipes that look
//   like "epmapper" but with slight variations (e.g., "epmapr", "epmappr",
//   "epmappe") to masquerade as legitimate RPC infrastructure.
//   Why it's Minimum Truth: There is no legitimate reason for a custom
//   application to create a pipe that almost-but-not-quite matches "epmapper."
//   This is exclusively an attacker technique (RPC deception / C2 masquerade).
//   Anchoring strategy: INTENT-FIRST (the typosquatting implies adversary
//   capability — the intent to deceive is the anchor)
//
// ANCHOR 4: HighRiskFramework Pipe Names
//   What it is: Known-bad pipe name fragments from specific C2 frameworks:
//   Cobalt Strike, Brute Ratel, Havoc, Mythic, Sliver, Covenant, Empire,
//   Meterpreter, and credential-dumping tooling.
//   Why it's (near) Minimum Truth: These names are either:
//   (a) Default pipe names shipped with offensive frameworks, OR
//   (b) Names used by credential-dumping tools
//   No legitimate enterprise software uses pipe names like "beacon_",
//   "meterpreter", "sliverpipe", "lsadump", "hashdump".
//   Important caveat: Unlike Anchors 1-3, these ARE names. A sophisticated
//   attacker can change their pipe names (malleable profiles). These names
//   catch default/lazy operators. They are NOT as reliable as regex patterns.
//   For this reason, HighRiskFramework pipes require OrgPipeCount <= 3
//   (rarity) to reach HIGH severity. Rarity + known-bad name = defensible
//   truth anchor. Known-bad name alone = high FP risk at scale.
//   Anchoring strategy: INTENT-FIRST (the known framework name implies
//   attacker tool usage)
//
// ============================================================================
// SCORING ARCHITECTURE
// ============================================================================
//
// MTDF base score for composites starts at 55 (the anchor is inherently
// suspicious). Reinforcement adds to the base. Penalties reduce noise.
//
// Scoring tiers:
//   ForkNRunHex:           Base = 85 (regex is specific, near-zero FP)
//   MojoDeviation:         Base = 75 (format deviation is specific)
//   EpmTyposquat:          Base = 70 (typosquat is specific)
//   HighRiskFramework:     Base = 75 (but requires rarity to reach HIGH)
//
// Reinforcement signals (all optional, never dependency):
//   R1: Rarity (OrgPipeCount <= 3): +25 (confirms targeted, not widespread)
//   R2: Suspicious parent process: +15 (Office, scripting host, LOLBin)
//   R3: SMB correlation (pipe seen on port 445/139): +20 (lateral movement)
//   R4: Near-time service creation: +10 (persistence indicator)
//   R5: Slow-service correlation (7d window): +6 (temporal deception aware)
//
// Penalties:
//   P1: Widespread pipe (HostCount >= 10): -15 (mass-deployment likely legit)
//   P2: System account (SYSTEM/LOCAL/NETWORK SERVICE): -10 (reduces priority)
//
// ============================================================================
// COUSIN TECHNIQUES (adjacent surfaces this composite doesn't cover)
// ============================================================================
//
// These require SEPARATE composites (different truth anchor / noise domain):
//
// COUSIN 1: SMB-only lateral movement WITHOUT named pipe
//   (e.g., SMB file drop + service creation without pipe usage)
//   → Covered by: SMB_Service_Lateral composite
//
// COUSIN 2: WMI-based remote execution (uses WMI objects, not named pipes)
//   → Covered by: WMI_RemoteExec composite
//
// COUSIN 3: Named pipe C2 on non-standard port (HTTP tunnel, DNS tunnel)
//   → Covered by: Outbound C2 behavioural scoring composite
//
// COUSIN 4: MediumRisk / LegacyRPC pipes
//   → Covered by: NamedPipe_LateralMovement_Router.kql (Router Rule)
//   → WHY NOT HERE: These require correlation to reach truth confidence.
//     Pipe name alone does not constitute Minimum Truth for psexesvc, remcom,
//     lsarpc, etc. — they have high benign overlap in enterprise environments.
//     Mixing them here would break noise suppression for Anchors 1-4.
//
// ============================================================================

let lookback = 7d;
let slowServiceLookback = 21d;
let nearSmbWindowMins = 10;   // [BUG FIX] was toint(timespan/1m) — unreliable in ADX
let nearServiceWindowMins = 20;
let slowServiceWindowDays = 7;

// ── CONFIGURATION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

let BaselineAccounts = dynamic([
    "NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM", "LOCAL SERVICE", "NETWORK SERVICE"
]);

let BaselinePipeFragments = dynamic([
    "eventlog","winsock","sql","postgres","mysql","oracle",
    "vmware","vbox","hyperv","docker",
    "chrome","msedge","brave","firefox","teams","onedrive"
]);

let SuspiciousParents = dynamic([
    "winword.exe","excel.exe","powerpnt.exe","outlook.exe",
    "wscript.exe","cscript.exe","mshta.exe","powershell.exe","pwsh.exe","cmd.exe",
    "rundll32.exe","regsvr32.exe","wmic.exe"
]);

// ANCHOR 4: Known C2 framework and credential-tooling pipe name fragments
let HighRiskPipes = dynamic([
    // Cobalt Strike & common malleable profiles
    "msse-","status_","msagent_","postex_","postex_ssh_","postex_shim",
    "beacon_","beacon","pipetst","cobaltstrike_","cs_","csession","cspipe",
    "searchtextharvester",
    // Mojo masquerade (some CS malleable profiles)
    "mojo.5688.8052.",
    // Brute Ratel / Havoc / Mythic / Nighthawk
    "bruteratel","badger","bager","demon_pipe","mythic","nh_",
    // Sliver
    "sliverpipe","sliver_c2","sliver_multiplayer","operator","multiplayer","sliver",
    // Covenant / Empire / PoshC2
    "gruntsvc","covenant","empire","emppipe","poshc2","jaccdpqnvbrrxlaf",
    // Metasploit / Meterpreter
    "meterpreter","msfpipe","msf_",
    // Credential tooling pipes
    "lsadump","cachedump","wceservicepipe","samdump","hashdump","credpipe","tokenpipe"
]);

// ── PHASE 1: MINIMUM TRUTH — Pipe Events (schema tolerant) ──────────────────

let PipeEventsRaw =
    DeviceEvents
    | where TimeGenerated >= ago(lookback)
    | where ActionType in ("NamedPipeEvent","NamedPipeCreated","NamedPipeConnected")
    | extend F = parse_json(AdditionalFields)
    | extend PipeName  = coalesce(tostring(F.PipeName), tostring(F.NamedPipe), tostring(F.Pipe))
    | extend FileOp    = tostring(F.FileOperation)
    | extend PipeLower = tolower(PipeName)
    | where isnotempty(PipeName) or ActionType =~ "NamedPipeConnected"
    | where PipeLower !has_any (BaselinePipeFragments)
    | extend EventKind = case(
        ActionType =~ "NamedPipeConnected", "Connected",
        FileOp =~ "File connected",         "Connected",
        FileOp =~ "File created",           "Created",
        "Unknown"
    )
    // ── TRUTH ANCHORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // ANCHOR 1: CS Fork-n-Run hex pipe pattern
    | extend ForkNRunHex = PipeName matches regex @"^\\\\\.\\pipe\\[0-9a-f]{7,10}$"
    // ANCHOR 2: Mojo browser IPC masquerade deviation
    | extend IsMojo          = PipeLower has @"\.\pipe\mojo."
    | extend MojoLegitShape  = PipeName matches regex @"^\\\\\.\\pipe\\mojo\.[0-9]{2,8}\.[0-9]{2,8}\."
    | extend MojoDeviation   = IsMojo and (
          (MojoLegitShape == false)
          or (tolower(tostring(InitiatingProcessFileName)) !in~ ("chrome.exe","msedge.exe","brave.exe","firefox.exe"))
      )
    // ANCHOR 3: Epmapper typosquatting (RPC deception)
    | extend EpmTyposquat = (PipeLower has "epmap")
          and (PipeLower !has "epmapper")
          and (PipeName matches regex @"^\\\\\.\\pipe\\epmap[a-z]{1,6}$")
    // ANCHOR 4: Known framework/cred-tooling pipe names
    | extend IsHighRisk = PipeLower has_any (HighRiskPipes)
    // ── Only keep rows where at least ONE truth anchor fires ───────────────
    | where ForkNRunHex or MojoDeviation or EpmTyposquat or IsHighRisk
    | extend
        Proc        = tostring(InitiatingProcessFileName),
        Parent      = tostring(InitiatingProcessParentFileName),
        AcctName    = tostring(AccountName),
        SuspParent  = tolower(tostring(InitiatingProcessParentFileName)) has_any (SuspiciousParents),
        AnonOrWeird = isempty(PipeName) or PipeName matches regex @"[^\x20-\x7E]"
    | project
        TimeGenerated, DeviceId,
        DeviceName  = tolower(DeviceName),
        AcctName, Proc, Parent,
        Cmd         = tostring(InitiatingProcessCommandLine),
        PipeName, PipeLower, EventKind,
        ForkNRunHex, MojoDeviation, EpmTyposquat, IsHighRisk,
        SuspParent, AnonOrWeird;

// ── PHASE 2: PRE-SUMMARISED PREVALENCE (safe join — small table) ─────────────

let PipeFrequency =
    PipeEventsRaw
    | summarize OrgPipeCount = count(), HostCount = dcount(DeviceName) by PipeName;

// ── PHASE 3: REINFORCEMENT — SMB correlation ─────────────────────────────────
//
// WHY THIS IS REINFORCEMENT, NOT MINIMUM TRUTH:
// An SMB connection near the pipe event increases confidence that the pipe
// is being used for lateral movement (remote execution via pipe over SMB).
// BUT: C2 pipes can exist on the local host without SMB. The absence of
// SMB does NOT invalidate the truth anchor. Therefore SMB is reinforcement,
// not dependency. If we required SMB, we'd miss local C2 pipes entirely.

let SmbPipeConnections =
    DeviceNetworkEvents
    | where TimeGenerated >= ago(lookback)
    | where ActionType in ("ConnectionSuccess","NetworkConnectionSuccess","ConnectionSucceeded")
    | where RemotePort in (445,139)
    | extend F = parse_json(AdditionalFields)
    | extend SmbPipeName = tostring(F.NamedPipe)
    | where isnotempty(SmbPipeName)
    | project
        SmbTime    = TimeGenerated,
        DeviceName = tolower(DeviceName),
        RemoteIP, RemotePort,
        SmbPipeName,
        SmbPipeLower = tolower(SmbPipeName);

// ── PHASE 3: REINFORCEMENT — Service creation (slow-and-low aware) ───────────
//
// WHY THIS IS REINFORCEMENT, NOT MINIMUM TRUTH:
// Service creation (Event 7045) near pipe activity suggests the attacker
// installed a service to facilitate pipe-based remote execution (classic
// PsExec pattern). BUT: Many legitimate services are created in enterprise
// environments. Service creation alone is not truth. Pipe activity alone
// is truth (for Anchors 1-4). Together they increase confidence.
// The 21-day lookback specifically defeats temporal deception:
// the attacker may have created the service days before using the pipe.

let ServiceCreation =
    SecurityEvent
    | where TimeGenerated >= ago(slowServiceLookback)
    | where EventID == 7045
    | extend DeviceName = tolower(tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]))
    | project
        SvcTime       = TimeGenerated,
        DeviceName,
        ServiceName   = tostring(ServiceName),
        ServiceFile   = tostring(ServiceFileName),
        ServiceAcct   = tostring(Account);

// ── PHASE 4: CONVERGENCE SCORING ─────────────────────────────────────────────

PipeEventsRaw
| join kind=leftouter PipeFrequency on PipeName
| extend OrgPipeCount = coalesce(OrgPipeCount, 0), HostCount = coalesce(HostCount, 0)
// Classify (for output clarity — does not change truth)
| extend PipeCategory = case(
    ForkNRunHex,     "CS_ForkNRun",
    MojoDeviation,   "MojoMasquerade",
    EpmTyposquat,    "RPC_Typosquat",
    IsHighRisk,      "HighRiskFramework",
    "Unknown"
  )
| extend KillChainStage = case(
    ForkNRunHex or PipeCategory == "HighRiskFramework" or MojoDeviation or EpmTyposquat,
        "Command & Control / Post-Exploitation",
    "Suspicious Named Pipe Activity"
  )
// SMB reinforcement join
| join kind=leftouter (SmbPipeConnections) on DeviceName
| extend SmbNear = isnotempty(RemoteIP)
      and abs(datetime_diff("minute", TimeGenerated, SmbTime)) <= nearSmbWindowMins
| extend PipeMatchesSmb = isnotempty(SmbPipeName)
      and tolower(PipeName) == SmbPipeLower
// Service reinforcement join
| join kind=leftouter (ServiceCreation) on DeviceName
| extend ServiceNear = isnotempty(ServiceName)
      and abs(datetime_diff("minute", TimeGenerated, SvcTime)) <= nearServiceWindowMins
| extend ServiceSlow = isnotempty(ServiceName)
      and abs(datetime_diff("day", TimeGenerated, SvcTime)) <= slowServiceWindowDays
// ── MTDF SCORING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Base score reflects anchor strength:
//   ForkNRunHex = 85  (regex is structural, near-zero FP)
//   MojoDeviation = 75 (format deviation is near-zero FP)
//   EpmTyposquat = 70  (typosquat intent near-zero FP)
//   HighRiskFramework = 75 (known names, some FP risk at scale, rarity required)
//
// Reinforcement adds on top:
//   R1 Rarity (OrgCount <= 1): +25 — targeted, not mass deployment
//   R2 Rarity (OrgCount <= 3): +18 — uncommon
//   R3 Rarity (OrgCount <= 10): +10 — below enterprise baseline
//   R4 Suspicious parent: +15 — scripting host / Office app spawned pipe
//   R5 SMB + pipe name match: +20 — lateral movement confirmed
//   R6 Near service creation: +10 — PsExec-style persistence
//   R7 Slow service (7d): +6 — temporal deception awareness
//
// Penalties:
//   P1 Widespread (>=10 hosts): -15 — not targeted
//   P2 Widespread (>=5 hosts): -8
//   P3 System account: -10 — reduces urgency (not legitimacy)
| extend
    BaseScore = case(
        ForkNRunHex,   85,
        MojoDeviation, 75,
        EpmTyposquat,  70,
        IsHighRisk,    75,
        55
    ),
    RarityScore = case(
        OrgPipeCount <= 1,  25,
        OrgPipeCount <= 3,  18,
        OrgPipeCount <= 10, 10,
        0
    ),
    SpreadPenalty = case(
        HostCount >= 10, -15,
        HostCount >= 5,   -8,
        0
    ),
    ContextScore = (15 * iff(SuspParent, 1, 0))
                + (20 * iff(SmbNear and PipeMatchesSmb, 1, 0))
                + (10 * iff(ServiceNear, 1, 0))
                + (6  * iff(ServiceSlow, 1, 0)),
    BaselinePenalty = iff(AcctName in (BaselineAccounts), -10, 0)
| extend FinalScore = tolong(BaseScore + RarityScore + SpreadPenalty + ContextScore + BaselinePenalty)
| extend Severity = case(
    FinalScore >= 95, "CRITICAL",
    FinalScore >= 75, "HIGH",
    FinalScore >= 55, "MEDIUM",
    "LOW"
  )
| where Severity != "LOW"
// ── HUNTER DIRECTIVE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
| extend HunterDirective = pack_array(
    strcat("[MIN_TRUTH] Anchor=", PipeCategory, " | Pipe=", PipeName, " | Kind=", EventKind),
    strcat("[SCORE] Final=", tostring(FinalScore), " | Severity=", Severity,
           " | Base=", tostring(BaseScore),
           " | Rarity=", tostring(RarityScore),
           " (OrgCount=", tostring(OrgPipeCount), ", HostCount=", tostring(HostCount), ")",
           " | Context=", tostring(ContextScore),
           " | Penalties=", tostring(SpreadPenalty + BaselinePenalty)),
    strcat("[PROCESS] Host=", DeviceName, " | Account=", AcctName,
           " | Proc=", Proc, " | Parent=", Parent),
    strcat("[KILL_CHAIN] ", KillChainStage,
           iif(ForkNRunHex,    " | CS_ForkNRunHex=TRUE (regex match — very high confidence)", ""),
           iif(MojoDeviation,  " | MojoDeviation=TRUE (non-browser or malformed format)", ""),
           iif(EpmTyposquat,   " | EpmTyposquat=TRUE (RPC deception pattern)", "")),
    iif(SmbNear,
        strcat("[SMB] Lateral movement vector: RemoteIP=", tostring(RemoteIP),
               ":", tostring(RemotePort), " | PipeMatch=", tostring(PipeMatchesSmb)),
        "[SMB] No near SMB correlation (local C2 pipe or pipe-over-non-SMB transport)"),
    iif(isnotempty(ServiceName),
        strcat("[SERVICE] Service correlation: ", ServiceName,
               " | Path=", ServiceFile,
               " | Near=", tostring(ServiceNear), " | Slow=", tostring(ServiceSlow)),
        "[SERVICE] No service creation observed (not required for Anchor 1-3)"),
    "[PIVOT] DeviceEvents | where ActionType has 'NamedPipe' and DeviceName == <host> | ±30m",
    "[PIVOT] DeviceNetworkEvents SMB 445/139 ±10m from pipe event",
    "[PIVOT] DeviceProcessEvents parent lineage from Proc column",
    "[CONTAIN] If C2/LM confirmed: isolate host, acquire memory triage, enumerate services/tasks/WMI subscriptions, reset credentials."
)
| project
    TimeGenerated, DeviceName, AcctName,
    PipeName, EventKind, PipeCategory, KillChainStage,
    Proc, Parent, Cmd,
    ForkNRunHex, MojoDeviation, EpmTyposquat, IsHighRisk,
    SuspParent, SmbNear, RemoteIP, RemotePort,
    SmbPipeName, PipeMatchesSmb,
    ServiceNear, ServiceSlow, ServiceName, ServiceFile,
    OrgPipeCount, HostCount,
    FinalScore, Severity,
    HunterDirective
| order by FinalScore desc, TimeGenerated desc
